this game was really fun with a pretty good story, go buy it.

Game is good and fun, but it needs A LOT of polish and It should be in EA, not launched...

The Good (mainly):
+Good variety of Jenins;
+Progress feels good (there is a good amount of grindy);
+There are good ideas on systems.

The Bad (the most urgent fixes):
- It needs A LOT of polish in its instances (you can't let different teams in different locations, it breaks the game);
- Some places looses it's "clickable use" out of nowhere (you have to restart the game to get it back to normal);
- There are a good quantity of Jenins, but It doesn't seem to let many possible variety on the teams compositions at the moment.

The game also needs more automatic interaction as an idle (like to hunt bosses and instances by it self).
Anyway, the idea of the game and it's system is 10/10 for me, but its current state is 5/10.

//The Last Cube World Player//

I am the last of the Cube World players.. I roam the world, music humming in a almost distorted sigh, child-like interest made manifest.. The era claws me in, cutting against my skin in a almost cuboid form. My froggy eyes stare deep into the wonderous possibilities, and I wonder.. I wonder once more.

My cubes are large, and weigh heavy.. Now - I can finally be a part of the World, I can get off my chair.. I can break these chains, and frolick.. For - I have done it, my childhood dream, my passion, I am an envoy for a time far away, I have finished.. Cube World.

